  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})+7(\\text{\u00a0arcsec\u00a0}x)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+7\\text{\u00a0arcsec\u00a0}x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
